# Workspace environment for the github_models smoke harness.
#
# GitHub Models is a managed cloud endpoint — there is no host knob.
# The deployment knob is the access token, which is interpolated into
# .jaato/profiles/*.json at profile-load time via ${GITHUB_TOKEN}
# substitution (see shared/plugins/subagent/config.py:_expand_string).
#
# How to get a token:
#   Option 1 (recommended): GitHub Copilot device-code OAuth
#       Run `github-auth login` and skip GITHUB_TOKEN entirely — the
#       provider picks up the stored OAuth token automatically. Leave
#       the line below commented out in that case.
#   Option 2: Personal Access Token
#       Create a PAT at https://github.com/settings/tokens with the
#       `models: read` permission (fine-grained PATs are auto-authorized
#       for SSO orgs; classic PATs need per-org SSO authorization).
#
# Optional: JAATO_GITHUB_ORGANIZATION attributes billing to an org.
# Set this if your access is org-scoped or you want enterprise billing
# attribution. Provider will use the org-scoped endpoint when set.
#
# The provider will error naturally if the token is missing or invalid
# (TokenNotFoundError / TokenInvalidError with actionable guidance).

GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_replace_me
# JAATO_GITHUB_ORGANIZATION=your-org-slug
